chived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-02-23T15:54:20Z","updated_at":"2025-02-23T16:03:42Z","closed_at":"2025-02-23T16:02:12Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10, Godot 4.3.stable, Vulkan 1.4.303, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU\n\n### Issue description\n\nfor example:\n\nvar original_input: Vector2 = Input.get_vector(&\"move_left\", &\"move_right\", &\"move_up\", &\"move_down\")\n\nor\n\nvar original_input: Vector2 = Vector2.ZERO\noriginal_input.x = Input.get_axis(&“ui_left”, &“ui_right”)\noriginal_input.y = Input.get_axis(&“ui_up”, &“ui_down”)\n\nif you press three keys at the same time (I know players will do), the get_vector function will miss the negative x or y input. if you press left, right, up at the same time, it didn't return Vector2(0, -1), but Vector2.ZERO instead.\nhowever, if you press left, right and down, it works fine and return Vector2(0, 1).\n\nby the way, i tried in 4.4 rc1, it didn't fixed it.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nvar original_input: Vector2 = Input.get_vector(&\"move_left\", &\"move_right\", &\"move_up\", &\"move_down\")\n\nvar original_input: Vector2 = Vector2.ZERO\noriginal_input.x = Input.get_axis(&“ui_left”, &“ui_right”)\noriginal_input.y = Input.get_axis(&“ui_up”, &“ui_down”)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nIt's easy to rewrite.","closed_by":{"login":"rock-roaster","id":200503162,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_Nveg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200503162?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rock-roaster","html_url":"https://github.com/rock-roaster","followers_url":"https://a